 157:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_tim.c **** 
 158:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_tim.c ****   [..]
 159:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_tim.c **** By default, after the Init and when the state is HAL_TIM_STATE_RESET
 160:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_tim.c **** all interrupt callbacks are set to the corresponding weak functions:
 161:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_tim.c ****   examples HAL_TIM_TriggerCallback(), HAL_TIM_ErrorCallback().
 162:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_tim.c **** 
 163:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_tim.c ****   [..]
 164:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_tim.c ****   Exception done for MspInit and MspDeInit functions that are reset to the legacy weak
 165:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_tim.c ****   functionalities in the Init / DeInit only when these callbacks are null
 166:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_tim.c ****   (not registered beforehand). If not, MspInit or MspDeInit are not null, the Init / DeInit
 167:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_tim.c ****     keep and use the user MspInit / MspDeInit callbacks(registered beforehand)
 168:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_tim.c **** 
 169:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_tim.c ****   [..]
 170:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_tim.c ****     Callbacks can be registered / unregistered in HAL_TIM_STATE_READY state only.
 171:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_tim.c ****     Exception done MspInit / MspDeInit that can be registered / unregistered
 172:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_tim.c ****     in HAL_TIM_STATE_READY or HAL_TIM_STATE_RESET state,
 173:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_tim.c ****     thus registered(user) MspInit / DeInit callbacks can be used during the Init / DeInit.
 174:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_tim.c ****   In that case first register the MspInit/MspDeInit user callbacks
 175:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_tim.c ****       using HAL_TIM_RegisterCallback() before calling DeInit or Init function.
 176:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_tim.c **** 
 177:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_tim.c ****   [..]
 178:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_tim.c ****       When The compilation define USE_HAL_TIM_REGISTER_CALLBACKS is set to 0 or
 179:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_tim.c ****       not defined, the callback registration feature is not available and all callbacks
 180:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_tim.c ****       are set to the corresponding weak functions.
 181:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_tim.c **** 
 182:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_tim.c ****   @endverbatim
 183:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_tim.c ****   ******************************************************************************
 184:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_tim.c ****   */
